# Citation metadata (Citation File Format 1.2.0). Read by GitHub's "Cite this repository" button
# and by Zenodo when it archives a release (version + date come from the release tag).
# Validate with: uvx cffconvert --validate
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Bayesify, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "Bayesify"
abstract: >-
  Bayesify assesses how well an academic paper follows Bayesian-workflow best practices. It
  ingests a paper (PDF) and produces a structured, evidence-linked report that grades the paper
  against a rubric of workflow components derived from the methodological literature (Gelman et
  al., Schad, Betancourt & Vasishth, Kruschke, WAMBS, and the MCMC/PSIS-LOO/SBC diagnostics
  literature), with per-step grades, suggestions, and transparent coverage and quality scores.
authors:
